[13.09223, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Postgres Copyprogram campaign\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: postgres-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.214\r\n\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\n   T1078      Valid Accounts                             [stealth]  step 1: valid accounts (weak postgres superuser)\r\n   T1059.004  Unix Shell                                 [execution]  step 2: COPY TO PROGRAM shell execution\r\n   T1048.003  Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol [exfiltration]  step 3: DNS-tunnel exfiltration\r\n   T1053.003  Cron                                       [execution]  step 4: cron persistence\r\n   T1543.002  Systemd Service                            [persistence]  step 5: systemd persistence\r\n   T1070.006  Timestomp                                  [stealth]  step 6: timestomp dropped files\r\n\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\n   ip     198.51.100.214\r\n   c2     update-postgres[.]example[.]cn\r\n   pool   stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]postgres[.]evil[:]3333\r\n   wallet 4A000000000000000000c5f08041507f\r\n\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S. National Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n"]
