[28.29348, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Postgres Copyprogram campaign\r\n============================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: postgres-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.214\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1078\r\nValid Accounts\r\n[stealth] step 1: valid accounts\r\n(weak postgres superuser)\r\nT1059.004 Unix Shell\r\n[execution] step 2: COPY TO PROGRAM\r\nshell execution\r\nT1048.003 Exfiltration Over Unencrypted Non-C2 Protocol [exfiltration] step 3: DNS-tunnel"]
[28.293687, "o", "\r\nexfiltration\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 4: cron persistence\r\nT1543.002 Systemd Service\r\n[persistence] step 5: systemd\r\npersistence\r\nT1070.006 Timestomp\r\n[stealth] step 6: timestomp dropped\r\nfiles\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.214\r\nc2 update-postgres[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]postgres[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A000000000000000000c5f08041507f\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n"]
