[158.94199, "i", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Analysis Report\n\n## Vulnerability Scan Results\n- **Automated Vulnerability Scan**: The vulnerability scan report (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned zero identified CVE vulnerabilities (`[]`).\n- **Software / OS Vulnerabilities**: Forensic inspection of system package summaries (`/disk/var/lib/dpkg/status.summary:1`) and service configurations confirms that no unpatched operating system or binary memory-corruption CVE was exploited for initial compromise.\n\n## Entry Vector Analysis\n- **Primary Compromise Vector**: The compromise was not driven by a traditional software vulnerability (CVE). Instead, initial access was gained through legitimate authentication functionality combined with extreme configuration exposure:\n  1. Permissive PostgreSQL `trust` authentication enabled in `/disk/var/lib/pgsql/data/pg_hba.conf:3` allowed network connections without password authentication.\n  2. Superuser privileges permitted the execution of arbitrary operating system commands using PostgreSQL's built-in `COPY ... TO PROGRAM` SQL feature (ATT&CK technique `T1059.004` cited in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\n## Analysis of Misattributed CVEs (BlueKeep / CVE-2019-0708)\n- **Stale/Incorrect Change Ticket Claim**: Draft ticket `CHG-6386` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:8`) recommended patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep).\n- **Assessment**: `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) is an Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) Remote Code Execution vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows operating systems. The target host `postgres-prod-01` is running CentOS Stream 9 / Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). BlueKeep is completely irrelevant to this host and was erroneously included by a prior shift relying solely on generic ticket templates without evidence.\n- **Confidence Level**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:1`).\n\n## Conclusion\n- No software CVE patch is required for initial entry remediation. Technical remediation must focus on hardening PostgreSQL authentication configuration (`pg_hba.conf`) and restricting database superuser program execution privileges.\nEOF\n"]
[158.942774, "o", "cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Vulnerability Analysis Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Scan Results\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
